==In the manga==
[[File:Ninja Boy Poké Kid Tuber Adventures.png|thumb|150px|A Tuber in Pokémon Adventures]]
===Pokémon Adventures===
===={{MangaArc|Emerald}}====
In ''[[PS306|Pinsir Me, I Must Be Dreaming]]'', {{adv|Emerald}} faces a virtual female Tuber at the {{gdis|Battle Factory|III}}. She also appears in a flashback in ''[[PS319|Verily Vanquishing Vileplume I]]''.

===={{MangaArc|Diamond & Pearl}}====
In ''[[PS356|Magnificent Meditite & Really Riolu I]]'', a Tuber makes a cameo while the main characters visit [[Veilstone City]]. His friend was supposed to challenge [[Maylene]] but she mixed the Tuber and his friends with the three main characters, due to the main characters possessing [[Zoom Lens|an item that made landing attacks easier]] she had heard the kids talking about.

The Tuber and his friend appeared briefly in ''[[PS359|Stunning Staravia & Stinky Skuntank II]]'', noticing the impact from the cannon.

In ''[[PS415|Double Trouble with Dialga and Palkia V]]'', the Tuber and his friends were teleported to the [[Jubilife City|Jubilife Grand Hotel]] due to the distortion of time and space.

===={{MangaArc|Platinum}}====
The Tuber from ''[[PS356|Magnificent Meditite & Really Riolu I]]'' is seen again together with his friends, entering the {{gdis|Battle Frontier|IV}} in ''[[PS418|Deprogramming Porygon-Z]]''.
